.TH EXP 3  "May 27, 1986"
.UC 4
.SH NAME
exp, expm1, log, log10, log1p, pow \- exponential, logarithm, power
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.ft B
#include <math.h>

double
exp(\fIdouble x\fP)

double
expm1(\fIdouble x\fP)

double
log(\fIdouble x\fP)

double
log10(\fIdouble x\fP)

double
log1p(\fIdouble x\fP)

double
pow(\fIdouble x\fP, \fIdouble y\fP)
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B exp
returns the exponential function of x.
.PP
.B expm1
returns exp(x)\-1 accurately even for tiny x.
.PP
.B log
returns the natural logarithm of x.
.PP
.B log10
returns the logarithm of x to base 10.
.PP
.B log1p
returns log(1+x) accurately even for tiny x.
.PP
.B pow(x,y)
 returns
.if n \
x**y.
.if t \
x\u\s8y\s10\d.
.SH SEE ALSO
math(3)
.SH AUTHOR
Kwok\-Choi Ng, W. Kahan
